--   An auxiliary lemma of the round-six development, published as a separate node because its proof is long or shared.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6CxNetF2`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.Cx.NetF2.memB_sound : ∀ (c : Code), okC c = true → ∀ w, memB c w = true → bitv w ∈ IntMul.Kappa.R6.Cx.NetF2.dec c
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Labels of the `h = 24` local program: codes over `𝔽₂^24` and a sound Boolean edge checker
--
--   A label code (`Code`) is one of
--
--   * `coord X`: `span {e_p : p ∈ X}`;
--   * `psp a b C`: `span {e_a + e_b + e_c : c ∈ C}` (a "pair span"; a line `⟨t⟩` is `psp p q {r}`);
--   * `perp t`: `⟨t⟩^⊥` (a triple `t`);
--   * `ext k`: boundary labels of stage two (decoded elsewhere).
--
--   Vectors are 24-bit naturals (`bitv`). `edgeB new old = true` implies
--   `NetComplexP8.EdgeOK (dec new) (dec old)` (`edgeB_sound`), with `finrank (dec c) = dimC c`
--   (`finrank_dec`). All functions are kernel-friendly (straight-line bit operations, SWAR popcount).
